{% from "docs-example.njk" import example %}
<h1 id="grid">Grid</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">Use CSS Grid for rows and columns. Add <code>grid</code> for display, a column utility for the tracks, and a gap utility for spacing.</p>
<h2 id="auto-fit">Auto-fitting columns</h2>
<p><code>grid-col-3</code> uses <code>repeat(auto-fit, minmax(270px, 1fr))</code>. It fits as many columns as the available space permits; it does not force exactly three columns.</p>
{% set markup %}<div class="grid grid-col-3 gap-16">
  <div class="docs-demo-item">One</div>
  <div class="docs-demo-item">Two</div>
  <div class="docs-demo-item">Three</div>
</div>{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Auto-fitting grid") }}
<table><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Generated declaration</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><code>grid</code></td><td><code>display: grid</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>grid-col-2</code></td><td><code>grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(331px, 1fr))</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>grid-col-3</code></td><td><code>grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(270px, 1fr))</code></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The minimum track widths are real minimums. A container narrower than 270 or 331 pixels can overflow. Choose the utility for your available content width, rather than treating the number in its name as a guaranteed column count.</p>
<h2 id="gap">Space between tracks</h2>
<p><code>gap-16</code> sets both row and column gap to one rem. These are the current spacer keys:</p>
<p><code>0, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 16, 18, 20, 24, 32, 40, 56, 60, 64, 80, 100</code>.</p>
<p>The values are rem-based Sass multipliers, not a general pixel parser. In the current scale both <code>gap-16</code> and <code>gap-18</code> resolve to one rem.</p>
<h2 id="sidebar">Sidebar layouts</h2>
<p>Combine <code>grid</code>, a sidebar utility, and a gap utility. Both sidebars use one <code>minmax(0, 1fr)</code> track below the <code>lg</code> breakpoint (960 pixels), then a fixed-width sidebar beside flexible main content. The breakpoint follows the viewport; allow enough container space for both tracks and the gap.</p>
<h3 id="left-sidebar">Fixed-width left sidebar</h3>
<p>Put the sidebar first. The docs use <code>grid grid-sidebar-left-lg-208px gap-32</code>: a 208-pixel left track from 960 pixels, with a two-rem gap.</p>
{% set markup %}<div class="grid grid-sidebar-left-lg-208px gap-32">
  <div class="docs-demo-item">Sidebar</div>
  <div class="docs-demo-item">Main content</div>
</div>{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Responsive left sidebar grid") }}
<h3 id="right-sidebar">Fixed-width right sidebar</h3>
<p>Put main content first. Use <code>grid grid-sidebar-right-lg-344px gap-40</code> for a 344-pixel right track from 960 pixels, with a 2.5rem gap. See the <a href="/ui/layouts/">posts and right-sidebar example</a>.</p>
{% set markup %}<div class="grid grid-sidebar-right-lg-344px gap-40">
  <div class="docs-demo-item">Main content</div>
  <div class="docs-demo-item">Sidebar</div>
</div>{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Responsive right sidebar grid") }}
<table><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Tracks from 960 pixels</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><code>grid-sidebar-left-lg-208px</code></td><td><code>208px minmax(0, 1fr)</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>grid-sidebar-right-lg-344px</code></td><td><code>minmax(0, 1fr) 344px</code></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h3 id="customize-sidebar-width">Customize sidebar widths</h3>
<p>Set <code>$sidebar-widths</code> near the top of <code>src/my-epic-css/_custom.scss</code>, then rebuild Sass. The fallback map in <code>_variables.scss</code> uses <code>!default</code>, preserving a map assigned before the library is imported.</p>
<pre><code>$sidebar-widths: (
  narrow: 208px,
  wide: 344px,
);</code></pre>
<p>Each map value generates both left and right utilities: <code>grid-sidebar-left-lg-208px</code>, <code>grid-sidebar-right-lg-208px</code>, <code>grid-sidebar-left-lg-344px</code>, and <code>grid-sidebar-right-lg-344px</code>. Keep the narrow sidebar for navigation and use the wider left sidebar for author profiles.</p>
<p>Map keys label the settings; widths and units form the class names. Add <code>medium: 280px</code> to generate both <code>grid-sidebar-left-lg-280px</code> and <code>grid-sidebar-right-lg-280px</code>. Update HTML when changing an existing width. The map replaces the individual left/right width settings.</p>
<p>Replace the former fixed right-sidebar and percentage left-sidebar utilities with the configurable utilities and a separate gap utility. The former small-sidebar helper is removed. The fractional helper is now <code>grid-md-1fr-4fr</code>: combine it with <code>grid</code> for <code>1fr 4fr</code> tracks from 820 pixels.</p>
<h2 id="containers">Containers and widths</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><code>wrapper</code></td><td>Five percent padding on each side.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>container</code></td><td>Centered container with the Sass-configured maximum width: 1040 pixels on this site, with a 1000-pixel library fallback. See <a href="/docs/wrapper-and-container/#customize-container-width">container customization</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>container-post</code></td><td>Centered container with an independently configured <code>$container-post-width</code>: 1000-pixel fallback and a 900-pixel custom setting. See <a href="/docs/wrapper-and-container/#customize-post-container">post container customization</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>w-100</code></td><td>Full available width.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>margin-auto</code></td><td><code>margin: 0 auto</code>, resetting vertical margins and centering horizontally where the available width permits.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>sm-w-25</code>, <code>md-w-50</code>, <code>lg-w-75</code></td><td>Examples of breakpoint-prefixed 25%, 50%, and 75% widths.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The generated width prefixes are <code>xs</code>, <code>sm</code>, <code>md</code>, <code>lg</code>, and <code>xl</code>, using the same <a href="/docs/flexbox/#responsive-direction">breakpoints as Flexbox</a>. Percentage widths combined with gaps can exceed the parent's available width; use the auto-fitting grid where it better fits the content.</p>
